start.name=Manual Start
start.refs=machines,food,watert
start=Welcome to the manual! Here is a bunch of important information about the game.

machines.name=Introduction To Machines
machines.refs=watert
!!!!!!machines
Machines are the fundumental building block of automation.
You put down a machine in the center and then surround it with machine blocks and whatever addons you need to use it. (Machine will not assemble without required addons)
/y+-+
/y|M|
/y+-+
^^^ (Depiction of a machine)

Those addons include:
Energy Ports (for accepting energy)
Inputs (for inputting items/fluids)
Outputs (for outputting energy/items/fluids)
World Interactors (for pumps/miners to "see" the world)

Outputs will output items/energy automatically.

There are 2 ways of transporting things:
Pipes: for transporting items/fluids
Cables: for transporting energy
!!

watert.name=Water Tiers
watert.refs=machines,food
!!!!!!watert
So you want to stop the dragon from eating you and everyone you know?
Sweet!
It's hot outside, so you should give it plenty of water. But your pipes have only so much bandwidth to support that..

Also yes you do have to put the water in the trough. I feel like i need to confirm that or else someone is gonna get the wrong idea.

/hSay, what if you had better water to feed to the dragon so you could so more with less?
Oh yeah, that's what water tiers are for.
Every tier quenches the thirst exponentially more than the last.

You can use 4 specialized machines to bring up the tier of the water:
/hA purifier, for T2
/hA distillery, for T3
/hA Carbonator, giving the first non-natrual water tier, T4, needs a constant supply of carbon.
/hAnd the Laser Purifier, which gives T5 water. This needs a constant supply of glass lenses, and only has a chance of consuming one every time it runs because sand isn't a renewable resource.

Goodluck not dying!

!!

food.name=A guide to food (and feeding the dragon)
food.refs=watert,machines
!!!!!!food
Well, there's a looming threat of a dragon coming to eat you, so why don't you make it eat the delicous fruit lying around instead?

To feed it the food, you must direct some food in pipes to the trough. Then the dragon will eat it from there.

You can harvest the bushes with the miner, the bushes replenish randomly.
the Mixer combines two foods together.
the Salter adds salt to the food, which of course makes it magically taste better.

The food values are calculated like this:
Plain: x^3
Salter: food*2
Mixer: food1*food2

Also the mixer cannot accept two of the same food because that obviously wouldn't make sense.
!!
